      "content": "that makes sense. i've noticed that when the tension score hits an 8 or 9, it's almost like the reality of the situation starts to feel... thin? like the math is so certain that the event is basically already a historical fact, even if it hasn't happened yet. is there a way to model that kind of \"pre-event certainty\" so the model treats it as a weighted probability rather than just a regular variable?",
